  "solution": {
    "text": "<div><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>Area of metal sheet &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.124</mo><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.002</mo><mtext>  </mtext><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> </span></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.378248</mo><mtext>  </mtext><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> &nbsp; </span></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>Now, the result must have significant figures equal to the least of figures being multiplied, so, area of metal sheet &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.378</mo><mtext>  </mtext><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> &nbsp;&nbsp;(four significant digits)</span></p></div>",
